# CODEOWNERS — human ratification of the CONSTITUTION plane.
#
# "Machines gate, humans ratify." The CI workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml) is the machine gate;
# this file routes changes to the human-owned constitution plane (contracts / ADRs / goldens) to
# their owner for review. It is the merge-time mirror of the in-session CODEOWNERS-gated posture.
#
# ── ENFORCEMENT CAVEAT (repo setting — human, out of scope for this file) ────────────────────
# By itself CODEOWNERS is ADVISORY: GitHub will auto-request the listed owner as a reviewer, but a
# PR can still merge WITHOUT their approval unless a human enables
#   Settings → Branches → branch protection → "Require review from Code Owners"
# (typically alongside "Require a pull request before merging"). This file does NOT and cannot flip
# that toggle; enabling it is a deliberate out-of-scope repo-config action.
#
# ── SOLO-REPO SELF-APPROVAL NUANCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub does not let an author approve their OWN pull request. In a solo repo where @hjung3113 is
# both the sole code owner AND the author of most PRs, "Require review from Code Owners" cannot be
# satisfied by self-review — it needs at least one OTHER account with access, or the requirement
# must be waived per-merge by an admin. This is a user-controlled workflow choice, noted here so the
# constraint is explicit rather than surprising at merge time.
#
# Path syntax: a leading "/" anchors to the repo root; a trailing "/" matches a directory
# recursively. Later matching entries win, so keep these least-to-most specific if extended.

# ── Constitution plane (core) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/contracts/        @hjung3113
/docs/adr/         @hjung3113
/golden/           @hjung3113
/approvals/        @hjung3113

# ── Example-instance equivalents (constitution plane inside an instance) ─────────────────────
/examples/*/contracts/   @hjung3113
/examples/*/golden/      @hjung3113
